cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite it as below."
title: "An Open-Source Educational Artifact for Wireless Packet Observability in Cyber-Physical Laboratories"
abstract: >-
  A software-first educational artifact with optional owned-device and
  receive-only hardware extensions for teaching reproducible wireless packet
  observability in cyber-physical laboratories. The default workflow is
  software-only: it generates deterministic synthetic packet traces, computes
  packet-level metrics, produces figures, and writes per-run manifests with
  SHA-256 hashes across four synthetic reference workload profiles W1-W4
  (configuration files wifi_like, ble_like, ieee802154_like, lora_sdr_like).
  Optional hardware extensions are restricted to owned or authorised devices and
  receive-only observation where legally permitted. Synthetic traces are not
  real radio measurements; the artifact does not validate the performance of
  Wi-Fi, BLE, IEEE 802.15.4, Zigbee, LoRa, or SDR systems. Version 0.1.1
  corrects the finite-span event-rate estimator to (N - 1) / (t_max - t_min)
  and adds independent, analytically derived regression tests.
type: software
version: 0.1.1
